+# IronClaude 5.0.0 human test guides
+
+These guides let a person check the 5.0.0 release by hand. Each guide covers one area, gives every step a Do / Expected result / Pass-Fail block, and cites the code line, `--help` output or recorded run that each expected result comes from.
+
+- `user/` holds the 16 guides for end users, operators and maintainers (D01-D16).
+- `sysop/` holds the 2 guides for system operators who control the Coder workspace env file or push to the fork's master branch (E01-E02).
+
+## How the guides are laid out
+
+Every guide groups its steps under three tiers, so you can stop after any tier:
+
+- **Tier A**: free, read-only checks that take seconds.
+- **Tier B**: steps that write files, always in a throwaway `HOME` or under `/tmp`.
+- **Tier C**: steps that use the Claude API, proxy credentials, real PRs or long runs.
+
+Each step heading carries one cost tag from the legend below.
+
+## Cost-tag legend
+
+The tags are listed from lowest to highest cost. "Highest cost tag" in the guide table is the highest tag on any step of that guide.
+
+| Tag | What the step needs or does |
+|---|---|
+| `[FREE]` | Read-only check that takes seconds. No API call. |
+| `[LOCAL-WRITE]` | Writes files, only in a throwaway `HOME` or a `/tmp` path. Some steps also download from the network (for example D01's codegraph tarball and pipx clone). |
+| `[CLAUDE-SESSION]` | Needs an interactive Claude Code session. Uses API tokens. |
+| `[API-LONG]` | Starts headless `claude` subprocesses. Runs take minutes to hours and use API tokens. |
+| `[PROXY]` | Needs operator-issued proxy credentials: `T2ProxyUrl`, `T2ProxyKey` and `T2Model0N` (`src/superclaude/cli/swarm/config.py:53-59`). |
+| `[EXTERNAL]` | Creates or uses state outside your machine: a pull request, an issue, a push or an operator-run service. Run one only on purpose, against a sandbox branch or a throwaway repo, and check that any PR URL points at `IronbellyOrg`. |
