+## Safety rule: throwaway HOME
+
+- Any step that writes files does so in a throwaway `HOME` or a `/tmp` path, never in your real `~/.claude`, `~/.claude.json`, `~/.codegraph` or pipx environment. The install and upgrade steps (D01) run every command through `env -i HOME=<throwaway> PATH=<throwaway>` with stub `codegraph`, `orca` and `orca-ide` commands, as the recorded run does (`c-e2e-run.sh` functions `mkenv` and `run`).
+- The sysop guides never edit the real `/etc/aidev02/aienv.d/defaults.sh` (E01 points `AIDEV_AI_DEFAULTS_PATH` at a temp file) and never publish to master while testing (E02 points `CCSESSION_MODELS_URL` at a candidate file and `XDG_CACHE_HOME` at a temp folder).
+- `[CLAUDE-SESSION]` and `[API-LONG]` steps run Claude Code with your real install, in a scratch project under `/tmp`. Such a session does not write only its own history. The installed hooks also write under your real `~/.claude`:
+  - the freshness hooks write `~/.claude/state/` and `~/.claude/logs/` at session start and on every prompt (registered at `src/superclaude/hooks/hooks.json:18,49`; paths set at `src/superclaude/hooks/scripts/freshness-session-start.sh:8-9` and `freshness-user-prompt.sh:8-9`);
+  - `auggie-flag-clear.sh` writes the same two folders after each auggie tool call (PostToolUse, `hooks.json:104`; `auggie-flag-clear.sh:10-11`);
+  - the codegraph session-start hook builds a `.codegraph/` index in the scratch git repo and appends to `${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/superclaude/codegraph-init.log` (`hooks.json:28`; `codegraph-session-start.sh:27-31`).
+- Skip `[EXTERNAL]` steps unless you mean to create that outside state. Their `gh` commands name the target repository explicitly: `IronbellyOrg/IronClaude` or a throwaway repo the guide has you create. None targets SuperClaude-Org.
